From 379d2b5b55aecf4fc7965c00d4ba1829e6bd8806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dashboard compaction: compact status row + Nibe cost-savings
 estimate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Compresses the Dashboard per Håkan's request: Perific One, Effektvakt,
EV-laddning and Nibe now sit side by side as small square status tiles
(CompactStatusRow/CompactStatusCard) instead of four full-width sections.
Nibe's detailed status card and history charts are retired from the
Dashboard entirely (NibeStatusCard removed) — full Nibe detail now lives
only on the /nibe page, which gained the "Lyxläge varmvatten" toggle
(NibeControls) that used to live on the removed card.

Adds a first cost-savings estimate for Nibe's active price-peak reduction
lever (decision.py's "reduced_expensive_price"), mirroring the Growatt
battery's Cost & Savings card in spirit but honestly scoped to what's
actually computable without a thermal/COP model: a degree-hour proxy
(core/nibe/savings.py) applied only to the one lever that genuinely reduces
consumption, using today's actually-applied heat-offset history and
already-cached spot prices. Surfaced as a compact "kr idag" figure on the
Dashboard tile and a full breakdown (NibeSavingsCard) with the model's own
assumptions spelled out on the Nibe page.

Backed by competitive research into other HA/inverter dashboards' compact-
tile patterns and prior art for heat-pump savings calculations (see
claude/dashboard-compaction-and-nibe-savings-forslag.md).

